@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.454 = private unnamed_addr constant [709 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the Python `requests` or `httpx` module that omit the\0A`timeout` parameter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `timeout` parameter is used to set the maximum time to wait for a\0Aresponse from the server. By omitting the `timeout` parameter, the program\0Amay hang indefinitely while awaiting a response.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport requests\0A\0Arequests.get(\22https://www.example.com/\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport requests\0A\0Arequests.get(\22https://www.example.com/\22, timeout=10)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Requests documentation: Timeouts](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user/advanced/#timeouts)\0A- [httpx documentation: Timeouts](https://www.python-httpx.org/advanced/timeouts/)\0A", align 1
